<title>GERMANY: CDU's Hintze calls for punctual EMU start.</title>
<headline>CDU's Hintze calls for punctual EMU start.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peter Hintze, general secretary of Chancellor Helmut Kohl's Christian Democrats (CDU), said on Monday the party continues to strive for European monetary union (EMU) to start on schedule on January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>Following a meeting of the party's leaders, Hintze said the CDU stands by the goals of a strict adherence to the stability criteria and a punctual start for EMU.</p>
<p>Hintze said Kohl has always said stability takes priority over the timetable, but a punctual start would also have stabilising effects.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
